            "type": "loki",
            "uid": "${loki_datasource}"
          },
          "editorMode": "code",
          "expr": "sum(count_over_time({cluster=~\"$cluster\", filename=~\"/var/log/(kern.log|syslog)\", node=~\"$node\"} |~ \"(?i)xid\" !~ \"Xid [(][^)]*[)]: (13|31|32|43|45)[,:]\" [$__range]))",
          "legendFormat": "Raw log lines (DCGM re-logs)",
          "queryType": "instant",
          "refId": "B"
        }
      ],
      "title": "Distinct incidents vs raw log lines",
      "type": "stat"
    },
    {
      "datasource": {
        "type": "loki",
        "uid": "${loki_datasource}"
      },
      "description": "One row per DISTINCT incident = a unique (node, gpu, pci, xid) combination. Dedup method: pull the raw XID log lines (kernel NVRM + DCGM), parse the XID code, the DCGM GPU index (\"for GPU N\") and the NVRM PCI address, then GROUP the lines by (node, gpu, pci, xid). Grafana's Group-by transform reduces each group to First seen (min timestamp), Last seen (max timestamp) and the number of re-logs collapsed. So the many DCGM re-logs of the same XID become a single incident row with a real first-seen time. NOTE: this table is built from log lines (direction=forward, capped at maxLines=5000 so the OLDEST lines — the true first-seen — are retained); on very busy ranges the 'Re-logs (sampled)' column is a sample, but the incident rows and first-seen times are still correct. Use the stat above for the authoritative (non-sampled) distinct count. NVRM kernel lines carry a PCI address (not a GPU index) so their GPU column is blank and PCI is populated; DCGM lines are the reverse. Benign/app-level XIDs (13,31,32,43,45) excluded; genuine hardware XIDs only. — Empty = healthy (no XID errors in the selected range).",
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "custom": {
            "align": "auto",
            "cellOptions": {
              "type": "auto"
            },
            "filterable": true
          },
          "mappings": [],
          "noValue": "✓ No XID errors — GPUs healthy"
        },
        "overrides": [
